    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27-a3">

                <pb facs="0102" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg32"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in Japan,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-04-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 23, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor to inform your excellencies of the arrival of the United States
                    steamers Shenandoah and Wyoming at this anchorage, and that I purpose to proceed
                    with those vessels to Osacca, leaving here about the 26th instant.</p>
                <p>With respect and esteem,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the
                            United States in Japan.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Their Excellencies the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministers for Foreign
                            Affairs,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Yedo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
